<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI3152-M5-WINDOWS-BUILD-BREAK>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI3152-M5-WINDOWS-BUILD-BREAK" ;
  triage:title "M5-ADMISSION-FIX-3 breaks the Windows build: unresolved crate::local_ipc_transport import on windows" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/local_ipc_transport/request_worker.rs:20 now imports `crate::local_ipc_transport::admission::{...}` (added by the M5-ADMISSION-FIX-3 join-deadline change). But crates/atm-daemon/src/lib.rs:28-29 gates the entire local_ipc_transport module behind `#[cfg(not(windows))]`. This produces a hard compile error (E0433: failed to resolve, could not find `local_ipc_transport` in the crate root) on windows-latest, confirmed via CI job logs for PR #722 run 30766398824. This directly contradicts arch-ctm's QA-3 claim that `just lint` and `just test` pass." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "daemon-shutdown" ;
  triage:severity "Blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-02T21:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S13 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-02T21:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI3152-M5-WINDOWS-BUILD-BREAK/m5-1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-08-02T22:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:progressNote "M5-ADMISSION-QA-4 (commit 3f200470): fixed. arch-ctm's M5-ADMISSION-FIX-4 removed local_ipc_transport/admission.rs entirely and moved the shared join-with-timeout primitive to a new crate-root module crates/atm-daemon/src/daemon_worker_join.rs, declared at lib.rs:15 with NO cfg gate (confirmed via grep -n \"mod daemon_worker_join\" lib.rs -- unlike local_ipc_transport at lib.rs:32 which is #[cfg(not(windows))]). request_worker.rs:1-5 now imports CompletionTrackedJoinHandle/JoinTimeoutPolicy/LOCAL_WORKER_JOIN_DEADLINE/join_with_timeout from crate::daemon_worker_join instead of crate::local_ipc_transport::admission, so the import no longer crosses the windows-excluded module boundary. Independently confirmed via gh pr checks 722 on head 3f200470: all 8 legs pass including 'Just lint (windows-latest)' and 'Test (windows-latest)' (run 30767976312). The E0433 compile error is gone." ;
  triage:progressNote "M5-ADMISSION-POSTMERGE-REVIEWERBACKED (integrate/phase-ai-31-33 @ c9ba04d9): reconfirmed fixed post-merge. Reviewer-backed recheck (req-qa, arch-qa, ruthless-boundary-qa independently corroborating; rust-qa-agent test/fmt pass but killed before full clippy completion) plus quality-mgr direct git/grep verification found the fix intact on the merged commit, matching origin/integrate/phase-ai-31-33. No regression." .

